# Compiled translations are committed, against the usual advice.
#
# UR04 asks for the interface in Spanish, and Django reads it from the compiled
# .mo, not from the .po beside it. Leaving the .mo out means a fresh clone
# serves English until somebody installs GNU gettext and runs compilemessages,
# and this project has no deployment pipeline to do that on its behalf. It was
# measured: on a clone with no .mo, twenty-one tests fail and every page comes
# out in English.
#
# The usual objection is that a build artefact drifts from its source without
# anybody noticing. `pages/tests/test_language.py` closes that: it reads every
# entry from the .po and asserts the running catalogue answers with it, so a
# .po edited without recompiling fails the suite rather than shipping quietly.
#
# gettext is therefore needed to *change* a translation, not to *run* the
# project.
*.mo
!locale/**/*.mo

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Course material kept locally for reference, not part of the project
course-material/

# Video production output. The scripts that build it are tracked; the audio,
# the slides and the rendered file are not, because they are large binaries
# that can be rebuilt with `python tools/video/build.py`.
tools/video/build/
*TEMP_MPY_*

# The narration recordings themselves. Audio files do not belong in a code
# repository; the finished video is published elsewhere.
tools/video/voice/*
!tools/video/voice/.gitkeep

# Browser automation session dumps
.playwright-mcp/

# Notes written for the live presentation, not part of the project
docs/diagrams/presentation-notes.md
docs/diagrams/cheat-sheet.md

# Operating system
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Graphify build output. The report and the graph are written to an archive
# outside this repository, but the extractor leaves a cache behind here.
graphify-out/
